SOP: CI/CD AUTOMATION AND DOCKER WATCHTOWER OPERATIONS (V2)
Organization: VULE ITS
Objective: Automate Docker Image updates using Label-based filtering and establish management operations on Ubuntu 24.04.
1. INITIALIZING THE MANAGEMENT SCRIPT
Using a Shell Script allows for easy configuration updates without the need to memorize or re-type complex commands.
Step 1: Create the script file
nano deploy-watchtower.sh
Step 2: Script Content
#!/bin/bash
# Watchtower Management Script for Ubuntu 24.04 - VULE ITS

echo "Setting up automated update system..."

# Remove existing Watchtower container (if any) to prevent configuration conflicts
docker stop watchtower 2>/dev/null
docker rm watchtower 2>/dev/null

# Run Watchtower with optimized parameters:
# --label-enable: Only updates containers with the specific allow-label
# --cleanup: Automatically removes old images to save disk space
# --schedule: Runs at 02:00 AM daily (Sec Min Hour Day Month DayOfWeek)
docker run -d \
  --name watchtower \
  --restart always \
  -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock \
  containrrr/watchtower \
  --label-enable \
  --cleanup \
  --schedule "0 0 2 * * *"

echo "Watchtower is activated and running in the background!"


Step 3: Permissions and Execution
Grant permissions: 
chmod +x deploy-watchtower.sh
Execute script:
./deploy-watchtower.sh
2. LABEL CONFIGURATION IN DOCKER COMPOSE
Add the following label to the docker-compose.yml file of each application you wish to enable for automated updates:
services:
  webapp:
    image: username/repository:latest
    labels:
      - "com.centurylinklabs.watchtower.enable=true"


3. ADMINISTRATIVE AND OPERATIONAL COMMANDS
Action
Docker Command
View Update Logs
docker logs watchtower
Stop Automation
docker stop watchtower
Restart Watchtower
docker start watchtower
Freeze Operations (Pause)
docker pause watchtower
Resume Operations (Unpause)
docker unpause watchtower
Immediate Manual Update
docker run --rm -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock containrrr/watchtower --run-once --cleanup [Container_Name]

4. CRITICAL TECHNICAL NOTES
Data Volumes: Ensure critical data (databases, uploads) is mounted to host volumes. When Watchtower updates a container, any data stored inside the container layer will be lost.
Private Registries: You must perform docker login on the server if your images are hosted in a private repository.
Disk Maintenance: The --cleanup flag is essential; it prunes the old image immediately after the new version is successfully deployed to prevent disk saturation.

